      "Language": "dan",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Knee pain is a frequent symptom facing the general practitioner. Some of the more severe differential diagnoses include bone infections and malignancy. We present a case report of a ten-year-old sports active and otherwise healthy girl with knee pain, which turned out to be haematogenous osteomyelitis."},
